From: Cedric Robert <cedric.robert@f2i-consulting.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:32:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Sized reads: the hot path of an ETP client moves to the
 sized forms

The reads a viewer makes most on a remote store now hand the proxy the
count they already use to size their buffers; every count comes from the
XML, none from the proxy, so an ETP proxy spares the metadata round trip
and an HDF5 proxy checks the extent.

- AbstractValuesProperty::getArrayOfValuesOfPatch gets a form taking a
  COMMON_NS::Span<T>: the proxy reads with the size, and the forced
  statistics count the buffer instead of asking getValuesCountOfPatch.
  The pointer form keeps its signature; both share one implementation,
  readValuesOfPatchInto<T, Buffer>, over the AbstractObject helpers
  overloaded for pointers and spans (patch 2).
- WellboreTrajectoryRepresentation (2.0.1): control points, MDs and tangent
  vectors, counted by getXyzPointCountOfPatch.
- WellboreFrameRepresentation: the node MDs (first value, as double, as
  float; 2.0.1 and 2.2 branches), counted by getMdValuesCount.
- IjkGridExplicitRepresentation (2.0.1): the grid points of a grid that is
  not truncated, counted by getXyzPointCountOfPatch; a truncated grid keeps
  the pointer read, its truncation points follow in the same buffer.
- AbstractIjkGridRepresentation: the pillar and column indices of the split
  coordinate lines (getSplitCoordinateLineCount) and the int8 temporaries of
  the pillar, cell and K-gap flags (the allocation's count).

The other representations (point sets, polylines, triangulated sets,
unstructured grids, 2.2 trajectories) follow the same pattern and remain
on the pointer forms for now.
